Sprintende Sprinter – License
Copyright (c) 2026 theStxve. All rights reserved.
Original code base: kyropytis (https://github.com/kyropytis).

IN SHORT: Sprintende Sprinter is a private project. You're welcome to read the
code and use the app yourself. Please don't redistribute it and don't make
money with it – just share the link to the project page instead:
https://github.com/theStxve/sprintende-sprinter
If you'd like to do something that isn't allowed here, just ask.

1. YOU MAY: read the source code and learn from it; install and use the app
   privately; build and modify the source for yourself as long as the result
   stays with you; fork the repository on GitHub to fix bugs or propose
   changes (issues, pull requests) – a fork serves only this purpose and apps
   built from it are not distributed; link to and recommend the project page.

2. PLEASE DON'T, unless you asked first and got an okay: distribute or publish
   the software or parts of it, not even for free (in particular APK files,
   app stores, download sites, mirrors, file shares, or copying code into other
   projects); publish or distribute modified versions or clones; make money
   with it, directly or indirectly (selling, ads, in-app purchases,
   subscriptions, inclusion in products or services, as part of a paid
   service); use the name "Sprintende Sprinter" or its logo for your own
   offerings; remove or change copyright or license notices.
   Permission is given by theStxve, easiest via the project page.

3. CONTRIBUTIONS: thanks for any help! If you contribute (e.g. a pull request),
   theStxve may include, adapt and publish it in Sprintende Sprinter under the
   project's terms, including future ones.

4. AUTHORS AND EARLIER VERSIONS: the original code base (first version of
   14 September 2026) was written by kyropytis; theStxve has developed the
   software since. kyropytis has agreed to this license for their own
   contributions. Up to and including version 1.3.1 the source code was under
   the MIT License. Since 10 November 2026 this license applies to the whole
   repository and to all versions and downloads offered here, including
   earlier ones. Anyone who received a copy under the MIT License before that
   date keeps the MIT rights for exactly that copy.

5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS keep their own licenses.

6. NO WARRANTY: the software is provided as is. Liability is excluded to the
   extent permitted by law.

7. Anyone who doesn't follow these rules may no longer use the software.
   German law applies.
